    "q-345106": {
      "dom_id": "step-q345106",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A series RCL circuit has a source electromotive force (EMF) of $12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\,\\text{V},$ a resistance of $24\\,Ω,$ a capacitance of $0.0625\\,\\text{F},$ and an inductance of $L=8\\,\\text{H}.$ Find the differential equation governing the amount of charge $q$ (in coulombs) on the capacitor at time $t$ (in seconds).\n\n*Hint: The voltage drop ${V}_{C}$ across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C},$ where $C$ is the capacitance measured in Farads.*",
      "worked_solution": "We have the following circuit diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14185497/assets/58cde9ddaa098a14ebb26bb70128f018f0c5892214815cc2d3057c9881a9546f.png)\n\nThe current $I,$ measured in amperes, is defined as the rate of flow of charge $q,$ measured in coulombs.\n\n$$\nI=\\frac{dq}{dt}\n$$\n\nKirchhoff's voltage law states that in a series circuit, the source voltage (EMF) equals the sum of the voltage drops.\n\nIn an RCL circuit, there are three voltage drops:\n\n- The voltage drop across the resistor is proportional to the current, with a constant of proportionality $R=24\\,Ω.$ So,\n\n$$\n{V}_{R}=24I=24\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}.\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{V}_{C}=\\frac{q}{C}=\\frac{q}{0.0625}=16q.\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the inductor is proportional to the rate of change of current, with a constant of proportionality $L=8\\,\\text{H}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=8\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}=8\\,\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dq}{dt})=8\\,\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, the differential equation governing the amount of charge $q$ on the capacitor is\n\n$$\n12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)=24\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+16q+8\\,\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{{d}^{2}q}{d{t}^{2}}+3\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+2q=\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
